R('<td>BlackRock won both; the 2023 rebid kept the same price</td>',
  '<td>Aladdin won in 2017 and again in 2023; the 2023 rebid kept the same price</td>')
R('<p>None of this is Studio-specific, and that matters less than it looks. Studio is sold for custom applications on Aladdin, and a buyer wants to know that another institution built on the platform and stayed; in custom-application land, proof from one firm counts even for a dissimilar buyer. Public pension funds, and firms whose filings or tenders already name BlackRock, can be named publicly more easily, and are the natural first candidates for a named Studio story.</p>',
  '<p>None of this proof names Studio. That matters less than it seems. Studio is sold for building custom applications on Aladdin, so a buyer wants to know that another institution built on the platform and stayed. For custom applications, proof from one firm counts even when the buyer is a different kind of firm. Public pension funds, and firms whose filings or tenders already name BlackRock, are easier to name in public. They are the natural first candidates for a named Studio story.</p>')
